<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link><description>India News Today: Get latest India news and breaking news from India on Times of India. TOI brings the top news headlines from India on Politics, Elections, Current Affairs and more</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-26T02:20:47+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/-2128936835.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:20:47 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[EPFO considers Rs 25,000cr war chest to stabilise interest payouts]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/epfo-considers-rs-25000cr-war-chest-to-stabilise-interest-payouts/articleshow/135197531.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135197531.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Employees’ Provident Fund Organisation is exploring the establishment of a Rs 25,000-crore Interest Stabilisation Reserve. This reserve aims to protect members’ interest payouts from corporate bond defaults and other market fluctuations. A report suggested that the fund should be built via surplus ETF gains and will invest in government securities. Historical performance indicates that this reserve can effectively manage interest rate stability.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/epfo-considers-rs-25000cr-war-chest-to-stabilise-interest-payouts/articleshow/135197531.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/epfo-considers-rs-25000cr-war-chest-to-stabilise-interest-payouts/articleshow/135197531.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T02:18:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Shiva Rajora</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135197536,imgsize-48170.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[BJP calls protest over Kharge’s ‘baap’ remark]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjp-calls-protest-over-kharges-baap-remark/articleshow/135197490.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135197490.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Congress president Mallikarjun Kharge's comment about Prime Minister Narendra Modi's father sparked widespread outrage among BJP members. Following the incident, the BJP announced nationwide protests against Kharge's remarks, labeling them indecent and offensive. Union home minister Amit Shah criticized Congress for personal attacks and blamed it on their electoral disappointments. Kharge also condemned the ongoing Special Intensive Revision of electoral rolls, describing it as a threat to democracy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjp-calls-protest-over-kharges-baap-remark/articleshow/135197490.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjp-calls-protest-over-kharges-baap-remark/articleshow/135197490.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-26T01:52:12+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135197501,imgsize-104164.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Give mayors real powers, ensure timely civic audits, urban body heads tell Centre]]></title><d