CDATA[PM Modi inaugurates RBI's Rs 169-crore data centre, cybersecurity institute in Odisha]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-inaugurates-rbis-rs-169-crore-data-centre-cybersecurity-institute-in-odisha/articleshow/135190459.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135190459.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-inaugurates-rbis-rs-169-crore-data-centre-cybersecurity-institute-in-odisha/articleshow/135190459.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pm-modi-inaugurates-rbis-rs-169-crore-data-centre-cybersecurity-institute-in-odisha/articleshow/135190459.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T17:46:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Kanchan Yadav</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135190668,imgsize-123520.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian American physician Navin Shah commits $525,000 to infectious disease program in Pune]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indian-american-physician-navin-shah-commits-525000-to-infectious-disease-program-in-pune/articleshow/135189974.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135189974.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Dr. Navin C. Shah has committed $525,000 to establish a new infectious disease program at BJ Government Medical College. The initiative aims to enhance research, medical training, and patient care for underserved communities in Pune. Collaborating with Johns Hopkins University, the program will focus on public health challenges like tuberculosis and HIV. Faculty and student exchanges are also planned to foster international cooperation in medicine.]]></des