eizes-boat/articleshow/135190136.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135190136.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[On Sunday, four Pakistani fishermen were intercepted by the Border Security Force in the Kutch district of Gujarat. Suspected of illegally fishing in Indian waters for crabs, they were detained following precise intelligence alerts. The crew members, hailing from Chach Jaan Khan village in Sindh province, are now under investigation as the BSF maintains vigilance over the sensitive border region to thwart unauthorized entries.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bsf-apprehends-four-pakistani-fishermen-in-kutch-seizes-boat/articleshow/135190136.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bsf-apprehends-four-pakistani-fishermen-in-kutch-seizes-boat/articleshow/135190136.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-25T17:17:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135190165,imgsize-246998.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Too deferential to govt': Former SC judge questions ex-CJI Chandrachud’s approach to appointments]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/too-deferential-to-govt-former-sc-judge-questions-ex-cji-chandrachuds-approach-to-appointments/articleshow/135189942.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135189942.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Congress flags judicial independence concerns over claims in ex SC judge's memoir]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/too-deferential-to-govt-former-sc-judge-questions-ex-cji-chandrachuds-approach-to-appointments/articleshow/135189942.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://